# The SITE-WIDE facts the client needs, published ONCE instead of per page.
#
# Measured over one preview of 1571 pages, 2026-10-02, these three payloads
# were inlined into the `<head>` of every page and were BYTE-IDENTICAL on every
# one of them:
#
#   | island                 | per page | total    | distinct payloads |
#   |------------------------|----------|----------|-------------------|
#   | `fa-translation-index` |   9.3 KB | 14.26 MB | 1                 |
#   | `fa-declared-kinds`    |    372 B |  0.57 MB | 1                 |
#   | `fa-site-links`        |    273 B |  0.42 MB | 1                 |
#
# 15.25 MB of one ~9.9 KB answer. The two obligations that come with loading it
# client-side instead are in `skills/ui/ui-core/ui-accessibility.md`
# §"A rendering built client-side owes two things the static one gave for
# free", and `assets/js/kg-render.js` is where this instance satisfies them.
#
# ONLY THE FIRST ROW IS HERE TODAY, and the other two are not an oversight.
#
# `getSiteLinks` and `declaredKinds` are read SYNCHRONOUSLY by
# `mountActionTiles`, inside an `init()` sequence whose own comments record its
# order as load-bearing — the icon row proxies the tile panel's button, and
# `mountInstanceGraphs` MOVES the node `mountDocumentIndex` inserts against.
# Moving them means either making that sequence wait on a fetch or re-entering
# its ordering. On 2026-10-02 four `ready-to-merge` PRs (#1804, #1805, #1808,
# #1819) were open inside exactly those functions.
#
# So: 0.42 MB + 0.57 MB does not buy that risk during a merge train; 22.34 MB
# did. THE CONDITION FOR MOVING THEM is that those PRs have landed and
# `mountActionTiles` can take its links asynchronously — at which point they
# are two more keys in this file and two more fallbacks in `getSiteLinks` and
# `declaredKinds`, not a different design.
#
# ONE FILE rather than one per fact, deliberately: these are one question —
# "what is this site" — and N files would be N fetches, N failure states and N
# chances for a page to be half-configured.
#
# RENDERED from the same `site.data.*` the islands were, so there is one
# declaration and two ways it reaches a page, never two lists. The prior art is
# `assets/harness/config.json` and `assets/harness/tiles.json` beside this
# file, and `scripts/staging-banner.ts:1-20`, which made exactly this move for
# the preview banner (bean `g196`) with the owner's approval.
#
# `fa-site-scheme` is NOT here, and that is not an omission. It is read by the
# first-paint snippet in `head_custom.html` — a synchronous script in `<head>`
# whose whole job is to set the colour scheme BEFORE the first paint. A fetch
# cannot be awaited there, so moving it would reintroduce the white flash the
# owner reported on 2026-09-24. `fa-translation-meta` is not here either: it is
# genuinely per-page (86 distinct payloads over the same 1571 pages).
# ── A NOTE THAT BELONGS HERE RATHER THAN IN `head_custom.html` ──────────────
#
# PROSE IN `head_custom.html` IS NOT FREE, and it is the only file in this
# repository where that is true. Its comments are HTML comments, not Liquid
# ones, so every byte is served on every page: measured 2026-10-02 over 2356
# pages, **1 KB of rationale there costs 2.36 MB published.**
#
# This change paid that before it measured it. The first draft of the comments
# explaining the move added 5845 B to `head_custom.html` and **gave back 62 %
# of the 22.34 MB saving it had just made** — a change that argued against
# inlining one payload per page, by inlining an essay per page.
#
# So the rule for that file: a comment there is a POINTER, and the reasoning
# lives in the artefact it is about — a `.js` docblock, which is served once
# and cached, or front matter like this, which is never served at all. The long
# comments already in `head_custom.html` predate the measurement; this is a
# reason not to add more, not a licence to delete theirs.
#
# This note is itself the worked example: it sits in front matter because front
# matter is free, and `head_custom.html` carries four lines pointing here.
#
layout: null
permalink: /assets/harness/site.json
sitemap: false
